{"id": "EUVD-2026-32802", "enisaUuid": "a5520ce1-0983-3e5e-aeea-faac89727977", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nf2fs: fix fsck inconsistency caused by FGGC of node block\n\nDuring FGGC node block migration, fsck may incorrectly treat the\nmigrated node block as fsync-written data.\n\nThe reproduction scenario:\nroot@vm:/mnt/f2fs# seq 1 2048 | xargs -n 1 ./test_sync // write inline inode and sync\nroot@vm:/mnt/f2fs# rm -f 1\nroot@vm:/mnt/f2fs# sync\nroot@vm:/mnt/f2fs# f2fs_io gc_range // move data block in sync mode and not write CP\n  SPO, \"fsck --dry-run\" find inode has already checkpointed but still\n  with DENT_BIT_SHIFT set\n\nThe root cause is that GC does not clear the dentry mark and fsync mark\nduring node block migration, leading fsck to misinterpret them as\nuser-issued fsync writes.\n\nIn BGGC mode, node block migration is handled by f2fs_sync_node_pages(),\nwhich guarantees the dentry and fsync marks are cleared before writing.\n\nThis patch move the set/clear of the fsync|dentry marks into\n__write_node_folio to make the logic clearer, and ensures the\nfsync|dentry mark is cleared in FGGC.", "datePublished": "2026-05-28T09:36:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:41:23", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1820a5814eadb8e63ab6c7c8d04e28ce49836be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ac93964658d0649337dcb3f6e38d77f8cdd86f3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8be551f538dc5b64183e27bd45a7a0795263f760", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7c6d30169b03307d27c4479563df79c08f3a746", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3e238bd1f56993f205ef83889d406dfeaf717a8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-46175", "GHSA-vwpg-8m6q-566g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3398815c-fac5-3cde-abcd-d22e73206a3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "da011cc0da8cf4a60ddf4d2ae8b42902a3d71e5f <8ac93964658d0649337dcb3f6e38d77f8cdd86f3"}, {"id": "39a78117-c95e-3a05-b8bc-f66d84ed86bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "da011cc0da8cf4a60ddf4d2ae8b42902a3d71e5f <8be551f538dc5b64183e27bd45a7a0795263f760"}, {"id": "45430d63-9103-3deb-9372-76dfc1e20f54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "5221bc6d-6536-3ba0-9c10-08970422dcc8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "56da54e5-83a3-3a6b-bbe4-52beb638f44a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "da011cc0da8cf4a60ddf4d2ae8b42902a3d71e5f <e7c6d30169b03307d27c4479563df79c08f3a746"}, {"id": "5be76ab5-9f00-3bce-a5c1-5e2ca1de6e0a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.7"}, {"id": "5e7842f4-4309-3a20-9868-e1eb424f1582", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "8bcd4c1a-0d40-3eaf-b1cb-33bc43991669", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "da011cc0da8cf4a60ddf4d2ae8b42902a3d71e5f <d1820a5814eadb8e63ab6c7c8d04e28ce49836be"}, {"id": "aa214ec3-77a4-3f0a-8b9a-9d30b3697ae9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e263db11-638b-3405-8004-96ef8c616312", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.7"}, {"id": "f08ab4fb-8302-3a16-a57d-ca1d1a574035", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.30"}, {"id": "f78d218b-ed7c-3f78-8ad9-ba29feddb157", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "da011cc0da8cf4a60ddf4d2ae8b42902a3d71e5f <c3e238bd1f56993f205ef83889d406dfeaf717a8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "16366c6f-bd99-3192-bdae-58546813e95b", "vendor": {"name